+# Heuresis usability pass — 29 Sep 2026
+
+This pass tightens the core flow without adding a new knowledge model.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Capture now defaults each new item to `reference`, with an explicit `Add to review` choice.
+- Parked Capture items retain their own reference/review state; older stored drafts safely load as reference.
+- Global Search opens the exact knowledge entry instead of only opening the topic, and identifies the field/note/knowledge block that matched where possible.
+- Added a canonical Knowledge Entry surface showing core fields, workspace knowledge, notes, tags, review state, review-method counts, recent review sessions, and readable connections.
+- Catalogue results and Catalogue Read Mode can open the canonical Knowledge Entry.
+- Connections now include a readable `Connected knowledge` strip and distinguish `links to` from `linked from`; connected entries can open the canonical entry surface.
+- Review scratchpad writing before reveal automatically records the `Hand-write` retention method for that card/session.
+- Review history groups grade + retention methods by study session so a card can show not only how often it was reviewed, but how it was reviewed.
+- Replaced user-facing `Raw connected entry` wording in the connection map footer with `connected reference entry`.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `node scripts/check-architecture.mjs` passes.
+- Modified TypeScript/TSX files pass TypeScript transpile/syntax diagnostics.
+- A full Vite build could not be run in the isolated environment because project npm dependencies were not present and package installation timed out. No dependency or package-version changes were made.
